    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repository, and its two tests both pass. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented so that `registrationDate` defaults to the server's current date when omitted and round-trips a supplied value in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field appears on both the create request DTO and the returned `Owner` DTO, and the OpenAPI generator produces it as a `LocalDate` serialized as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) entity field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When the incoming payload has no `registrationDate`, it's defaulted to `LocalDate.now()` before mapping/saving; a supplied value is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres) for consistency.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass, and the full suite is green.",
